1
00:00:02,120 --> 00:00:04,440
THIS SHOW IS CREATED
FOR ENTERTAINMENT PURPOSES ONLY

2
00:00:04,520 --> 00:00:06,520
THE CHARACTERS, BEHAVIORS
AND EVENTS ARE FICTITIOUS

3
00:00:06,600 --> 00:00:08,560
THEY ARE NOT INTENDED
TO DEFAME OR CAUSE DAMAGE

4
00:00:08,640 --> 00:00:10,920
TO ANY ORGANIZATION OR INDIVIDUAL
VIEWER DISCRETION IS ADVISED

5
00:02:27,200 --> 00:02:28,200
<i>Definitely not an amateur.</i>

6
00:02:29,440 --> 00:02:30,680
<i>One shot, two dead.</i>

7
00:02:35,480 --> 00:02:38,640
<i>That woman who saw you.</i>
<i>She'll become a witness.</i>

8
00:02:39,600 --> 00:02:40,960
Go shut her mouth.

9
00:02:41,040 --> 00:02:43,200
I don't kill ordinary people.

10
00:02:43,280 --> 00:02:45,200
<i>You shouldn't have helped her.</i>

11
00:02:45,800 --> 00:02:46,720
She's not involved.

12
00:02:46,800 --> 00:02:47,680
Gun!

13
00:02:47,760 --> 00:02:48,920
Hey. Hey!

14
00:02:49,000 --> 00:02:49,880
Stop!

15
00:03:15,840 --> 00:03:18,280
Hey… I'm here.

16
00:03:19,160 --> 00:03:22,560
I was scared they'd come back,
so I went and hid over there.

17
00:03:23,840 --> 00:03:24,960
Okay, get in the car.

18
00:03:58,680 --> 00:04:00,040
Stay here for the time being.

19
00:04:02,760 --> 00:04:05,720
How much longer do we have to hide?

20
00:04:05,800 --> 00:04:07,320
Until they can't find you.

21
00:04:23,040 --> 00:04:25,960
What if they do find me?

22
00:04:30,840 --> 00:04:32,400
They'll have to get through me first.

23
00:04:37,840 --> 00:04:38,960
Use this

24
00:04:39,600 --> 00:04:40,800
for whatever you need.

25
00:04:44,840 --> 00:04:46,440
Do you do this for everyone?

26
00:04:51,480 --> 00:04:52,600
No.

27
00:05:11,760 --> 00:05:14,520
Intel points directly to the sniper.

28
00:05:16,840 --> 00:05:18,560
MR. GUNMET PHENGSAP

29
00:05:23,400 --> 00:05:24,320
What is it?

30
00:05:33,280 --> 00:05:34,240
Gun?

31
00:05:38,360 --> 00:05:39,880
They killed his grandmother.

32
00:05:40,920 --> 00:05:42,880
He's definitely not going
to let this slide.

33
00:05:44,240 --> 00:05:47,240
Form a team to locate him
as quickly as possible.

34
00:05:47,320 --> 00:05:48,560
Yes, sir.

35
00:06:15,520 --> 00:06:17,280
I bought some essentials.

36
00:06:18,880 --> 00:06:20,400
Not sure how long you'll stay.

37
00:06:29,760 --> 00:06:32,040
You know my size?

38
00:06:33,920 --> 00:06:35,160
Just guessed.

39
00:06:42,560 --> 00:06:43,760
There's no kitchen here.

40
00:06:44,800 --> 00:06:46,640
If you're hungry,
just microwave something.

41
00:06:49,920 --> 00:06:51,600
What about you?

42
00:06:52,200 --> 00:06:53,600
I can take care of myself.

43
00:07:21,000 --> 00:07:22,080
Grandma Lek

44
00:07:23,000 --> 00:07:24,920
was very proud of you.

45
00:07:28,160 --> 00:07:29,320
She was the only one

46
00:07:30,560 --> 00:07:31,800
who felt that way.

47
00:07:33,080 --> 00:07:34,000
That's not true.

48
00:07:39,920 --> 00:07:42,560
Someone who risks their life
to save others

49
00:07:43,280 --> 00:07:44,560
isn't a bad person.

50
00:07:51,080 --> 00:07:52,200
Try on the clothes.

51
00:07:52,720 --> 00:07:54,360
If they don't fit, I’ll exchange them.

52
00:07:58,560 --> 00:07:59,400
‎Thank you.

53
00:08:21,560 --> 00:08:23,960
I won't let it end like this, Grandma.

54
00:08:51,240 --> 00:08:52,400
What's the update?

55
00:08:52,480 --> 00:08:54,120
<i>We found Gun.</i>

56
00:10:05,000 --> 00:10:06,040
Damn it!

57
00:10:24,680 --> 00:10:25,520
Whoa.

58
00:11:05,640 --> 00:11:06,720
You're really doing this?

59
00:11:06,800 --> 00:11:10,040
Damn right. Nobody’s going anywhere now.

60
00:11:12,600 --> 00:11:13,440
Shit.

61
00:11:14,080 --> 00:11:15,120
Someone's losing an arm.

62
00:11:17,440 --> 00:11:18,440
Hey!

63
00:11:47,000 --> 00:11:47,880
Wait!

64
00:11:52,360 --> 00:11:53,760
I just want to talk.

65
00:12:01,880 --> 00:12:03,280
<i>You killed James and Tongyang.</i>

66
00:12:04,360 --> 00:12:06,880
You hated what they did,
yet you did the same thing.

67
00:12:11,320 --> 00:12:12,880
You can take this bag.

68
00:12:17,280 --> 00:12:18,720
Are you trying to bribe me?

69
00:12:18,800 --> 00:12:20,680
If you're worried
about getting into trouble,

70
00:12:21,920 --> 00:12:23,840
split it with your team.

71
00:12:24,720 --> 00:12:26,240
They're used to dirty money anyway.

72
00:12:29,520 --> 00:12:30,600
I know

73
00:12:31,800 --> 00:12:33,400
why you left the force.

74
00:12:33,480 --> 00:12:35,040
But don't lump us all together.

75
00:12:35,560 --> 00:12:37,200
Don't look down on me.

76
00:12:38,400 --> 00:12:39,880
I'm not naive.

77
00:12:40,960 --> 00:12:42,400
I'm just speaking the truth.

78
00:12:44,240 --> 00:12:45,200
Gun.

79
00:12:45,840 --> 00:12:47,920
The reason I joined the force

80
00:12:48,560 --> 00:12:50,000
was to root out corruption.

81
00:12:50,840 --> 00:12:52,720
To bring those traitorous
scumbags to justice.

82
00:12:53,880 --> 00:12:56,600
I will never take
a single baht of blood money.

83
00:12:58,480 --> 00:13:01,560
You say you're here to fight corruption
and serve the country,

84
00:13:02,720 --> 00:13:04,080
but you already know, don't you?

85
00:13:04,160 --> 00:13:06,880
Tongyang and his son are the masterminds
behind these scam operations.

86
00:13:06,960 --> 00:13:08,960
How many millions
have they stolen from Thai people?

87
00:13:09,040 --> 00:13:10,600
Are you just going to let them?

88
00:13:10,680 --> 00:13:12,040
Some people lost everything.

89
00:13:12,120 --> 00:13:14,360
If it were your family,
how would you feel?

90
00:13:14,440 --> 00:13:16,520
But you have to draw the line.

91
00:13:17,080 --> 00:13:20,040
They broke the law,
so you use the law to deal with them.

92
00:13:21,400 --> 00:13:25,120
-You can't play God with people's lives.
-And how can you be sure

93
00:13:26,280 --> 00:13:27,680
the law still has any power?

94
00:13:30,000 --> 00:13:31,240
The only reason

95
00:13:31,760 --> 00:13:33,520
Tongyang could still operate in Thailand

96
00:13:34,880 --> 00:13:37,000
was because officials
backed him, wasn't it?

97
00:13:39,960 --> 00:13:41,120
But you broke the law.

98
00:13:41,200 --> 00:13:42,560
But I actually saved people.

99
00:13:45,240 --> 00:13:46,440
Which side do you choose?

100
00:13:52,080 --> 00:13:52,960
Fine!

101
00:13:56,120 --> 00:13:57,720
To eliminate the problem at its source,

102
00:13:59,440 --> 00:14:00,760
you have to kill the mastermind.

103
00:14:03,760 --> 00:14:04,920
Who are you working for?

104
00:14:27,560 --> 00:14:30,320
Hey. Don't move.

105
00:14:32,600 --> 00:14:33,720
Get out of my way.

106
00:14:49,040 --> 00:14:50,000
Sir!

107
00:14:56,800 --> 00:14:59,960
Gun was caught by the police,
but he managed to escape.

108
00:15:24,880 --> 00:15:26,760
I told you guys

109
00:15:27,360 --> 00:15:28,320
he’s skilled.

110
00:15:29,440 --> 00:15:30,840
Way more skilled than you two.

111
00:15:33,760 --> 00:15:34,640
Boss,

112
00:15:35,680 --> 00:15:39,600
Gun now knows the real reason
you had Tongyang killed.

113
00:15:43,040 --> 00:15:44,600
And what do you think

114
00:15:45,720 --> 00:15:47,120
he's going to do?

115
00:15:47,880 --> 00:15:49,120
If it were me,

116
00:15:50,120 --> 00:15:51,480
I’d come back.

117
00:15:51,560 --> 00:15:52,400
Correct.

118
00:15:53,880 --> 00:15:55,960
A man who has lost everything

119
00:15:56,040 --> 00:15:57,920
has nothing left to fear.

120
00:15:58,000 --> 00:16:00,120
-Then we should finish the job.
-No.

121
00:16:00,200 --> 00:16:01,880
You're just going to leave him be, Boss?

122
00:16:01,960 --> 00:16:04,760
You seem to be in quite a hurry, huh?

123
00:16:05,640 --> 00:16:08,000
Well, he's a threat to you, Boss.

124
00:16:08,720 --> 00:16:11,080
Or are you afraid he's a threat to you?

125
00:16:13,800 --> 00:16:14,760
Hey.

126
00:16:16,720 --> 00:16:18,520
I'm the one who decides

127
00:16:20,360 --> 00:16:23,040
when the hell he dies, not you.

128
00:17:09,520 --> 00:17:13,119
My parents passed away…

129
00:17:15,280 --> 00:17:16,920
in a car crash.

130
00:17:18,880 --> 00:17:22,280
I survived the accident,

131
00:17:24,079 --> 00:17:25,920
so I grew up in an orphanage.

132
00:17:52,040 --> 00:17:55,640
The food's ready. Let me plate it for you.

133
00:18:10,840 --> 00:18:11,720
Welcome.

134
00:18:19,600 --> 00:18:20,920
Gold members only.

135
00:18:21,000 --> 00:18:22,320
Why's that, sir?

136
00:18:22,400 --> 00:18:25,000
Don't ask questions, just do as I say.

137
00:18:25,080 --> 00:18:25,960
Yes.

138
00:18:26,960 --> 00:18:28,160
Welcome, sir.

139
00:18:52,320 --> 00:18:53,920
You really think he’s coming back?

140
00:18:55,880 --> 00:18:59,200
I didn't just think.
I've prepared everything.

141
00:19:01,920 --> 00:19:03,840
Or are you actually just scared?

142
00:19:04,800 --> 00:19:07,400
What did you just say? Huh?

143
00:19:09,680 --> 00:19:13,600
People who throw their weight around
are usually insecure.

144
00:19:14,960 --> 00:19:18,040
Go upstairs and guard the boss.
I'm in charge down here.

145
00:19:20,400 --> 00:19:23,440
I had to come down here
because the boss doesn't trust you.

146
00:19:23,520 --> 00:19:26,760
Asshole! This is my domain, got it?

147
00:19:26,840 --> 00:19:28,800
Don't ever think you're better than me.

148
00:19:31,360 --> 00:19:32,560
Hey. Hey!

149
00:19:32,640 --> 00:19:34,120
Hey.

150
00:19:35,560 --> 00:19:37,040
What are you doing here?

151
00:19:38,280 --> 00:19:40,720
My friend told me to come here
and apply for membership.

152
00:19:40,800 --> 00:19:44,040
I saw you arguing,
so I didn't dare come closer.

153
00:19:46,440 --> 00:19:48,480
Don't act suspicious like that next time.

154
00:19:49,280 --> 00:19:50,080
Yes.

155
00:19:50,160 --> 00:19:51,440
Go to the front counter.

156
00:19:53,720 --> 00:19:57,320
Yes, thank you, sir.

157
00:19:57,400 --> 00:20:00,680
Pathetic. You can't even read
a simple situation like that.

158
00:20:02,040 --> 00:20:03,400
You're an idiot.

159
00:20:14,920 --> 00:20:16,240
That feels great.

160
00:20:42,360 --> 00:20:43,520
Hey, hold up.

161
00:20:48,760 --> 00:20:50,000
Take off that cap.

162
00:20:58,920 --> 00:21:02,120
Whoa, man. How did you get this drunk?

163
00:21:02,200 --> 00:21:04,520
Your wife told me to take you home.

164
00:21:20,880 --> 00:21:22,280
Does that feel good?

165
00:21:23,240 --> 00:21:24,640
Feels amazing.

166
00:21:27,400 --> 00:21:28,480
-A little more.
-A little more?

167
00:21:28,560 --> 00:21:29,400
Yeah.

168
00:21:30,160 --> 00:21:31,560
Just a tiny bit more.

169
00:21:31,640 --> 00:21:33,360
Stop it…

170
00:21:58,720 --> 00:22:00,520
Who the hell is that?

171
00:22:06,680 --> 00:22:10,160
Mod, go check
who’s at the door for me, will you?

172
00:22:10,240 --> 00:22:12,800
-Sure, be right back.
-Yeah.

173
00:22:25,400 --> 00:22:26,480
Who is it?

174
00:22:39,640 --> 00:22:40,480
Hey.

175
00:22:41,600 --> 00:22:43,960
I asked who it is. What do you want?

176
00:22:45,760 --> 00:22:46,680
Huh?

177
00:22:58,840 --> 00:22:59,720
Hey!

178
00:23:01,400 --> 00:23:03,760
Hey. Hey.

179
00:23:03,840 --> 00:23:07,040
Let's be reasonable here. We can talk.

180
00:23:08,480 --> 00:23:09,480
Hey.

181
00:23:09,560 --> 00:23:10,720
Someone told me

182
00:23:12,000 --> 00:23:15,720
you ordered the hit on Tongyang
so you could control everything.

183
00:23:16,360 --> 00:23:19,720
Come on. It’s just business.

184
00:23:19,800 --> 00:23:21,880
Every territory has its boss.

185
00:23:21,960 --> 00:23:24,640
He crossed the line, so I had
to make an example of him.

186
00:23:25,840 --> 00:23:27,920
Then why didn't you say that

187
00:23:28,640 --> 00:23:30,000
when you hired me to kill him?

188
00:23:32,440 --> 00:23:34,000
Don't make this so difficult.

189
00:23:34,520 --> 00:23:36,680
Come work with me.

190
00:23:36,760 --> 00:23:40,440
I promise to help you destroy
the bastards ruining this country.

191
00:23:40,520 --> 00:23:43,080
I know

192
00:23:43,160 --> 00:23:46,200
you hate corrupt,
scumbag politicians and officials.

193
00:23:46,720 --> 00:23:47,800
I'll help you end them.

194
00:23:47,880 --> 00:23:51,520
Helping you makes me scum too.

195
00:23:52,800 --> 00:23:57,120
And being a hitman
doesn't make you scum, huh?

196
00:23:57,200 --> 00:24:00,080
I'm fine with being scum
because I kill bad guys.

197
00:24:01,520 --> 00:24:03,960
But I won't work with the guy
who had my grandma killed.

198
00:24:04,040 --> 00:24:05,120
-Gun! Drop your gun!
-Hey!

199
00:24:05,200 --> 00:24:06,480
-You drop yours!
-Hey, hey.

200
00:24:06,560 --> 00:24:07,480
-I'll shoot him!
-Drop it!

201
00:24:07,560 --> 00:24:08,680
You drop it!

202
00:24:08,760 --> 00:24:09,680
-Hey.
-I said drop the gun!

203
00:24:09,760 --> 00:24:10,800
-Hey, hey.
-Drop it or I'll shoot!

204
00:24:10,880 --> 00:24:12,040
Calm down!

205
00:24:12,120 --> 00:24:13,640
Let's talk this out.

206
00:24:13,720 --> 00:24:15,240
Tell him to drop the gun.

207
00:24:16,800 --> 00:24:17,960
Won't you untie me first?

208
00:24:18,920 --> 00:24:22,160
-Tell him to drop the gun!
-Drop the gun. Drop it!

209
00:24:30,600 --> 00:24:31,800
Now untie me.

210
00:24:32,440 --> 00:24:33,760
Tell me first.

211
00:24:35,240 --> 00:24:36,720
Who went after my grandma?

212
00:24:47,000 --> 00:24:47,880
Answer me!

213
00:24:47,960 --> 00:24:50,200
-Answer him, damn it.
-I killed your grandma!

214
00:24:50,280 --> 00:24:51,080
You bastard!

215
00:24:53,320 --> 00:24:54,520
Hey, calm down! Wait!

216
00:24:59,240 --> 00:25:00,240
Holy shit!

217
00:25:00,960 --> 00:25:02,640
Hey, untie me first!

218
00:25:15,280 --> 00:25:18,600
Deactivate the bomb and untie me
right now, or we're both dead!

219
00:25:19,880 --> 00:25:21,400
Get over here and help me now.

220
00:25:47,360 --> 00:25:48,520
Hurry.

221
00:25:48,600 --> 00:25:50,320
Untie me and get this bomb off me!

222
00:25:52,600 --> 00:25:53,720
Come on.

223
00:26:10,920 --> 00:26:12,840
Time's almost up! Hurry!

224
00:26:20,720 --> 00:26:23,160
Hurry! Time's running out!

225
00:26:28,720 --> 00:26:30,320
Hurry!

226
00:26:33,640 --> 00:26:35,080
‎STAFF ONLY

227
00:26:48,200 --> 00:26:49,680
Damn, it didn't explode.

228
00:26:51,840 --> 00:26:53,560
-Untie me right now.
-Untie the boss.

229
00:26:53,640 --> 00:26:54,760
-Hurry.
-Boss!

230
00:26:54,840 --> 00:26:55,800
Ugh.

231
00:26:56,880 --> 00:26:57,800
Hurry up.

232
00:26:58,760 --> 00:27:00,080
-And get going.
-Let's go!

233
00:27:00,160 --> 00:27:01,320
-Move.
-Let's go, boss.

234
00:27:01,400 --> 00:27:03,120
-He might come back.
-Let's go!

235
00:27:03,200 --> 00:27:04,600
‎Come on, Boss.

236
00:27:05,360 --> 00:27:06,960
Boss.

237
00:27:07,040 --> 00:27:09,320
-This guy's really in the way.
-Come, Boss.

238
00:27:09,400 --> 00:27:10,920
Hey. Drag him along too.

239
00:27:13,040 --> 00:27:14,880
Mark, get up. Let's go.

240
00:27:15,520 --> 00:27:16,400
Come on.

241
00:27:23,280 --> 00:27:26,080
Hey, watch the rear. Is he following us?

242
00:27:29,240 --> 00:27:30,080
Easy.

243
00:27:30,160 --> 00:27:31,440
-This way.
-Right this way.

244
00:27:35,840 --> 00:27:37,400
Ouch! Move fast.

245
00:28:11,200 --> 00:28:14,440
<i>I checked the intel.</i>
<i>Sarawut was telling the truth.</i>

246
00:28:15,320 --> 00:28:16,880
<i>Seehan is making big moves.</i>

247
00:28:17,400 --> 00:28:19,000
<i>Someone must be backing him up.</i>

248
00:28:19,080 --> 00:28:19,880
‎METHEE

249
00:28:19,960 --> 00:28:20,760
‎GUN

250
00:28:20,840 --> 00:28:24,080
<i>I have contacts in intelligence.</i>
<i>I'll gather details for you.</i>

251
00:28:40,600 --> 00:28:42,120
Kill Gun for me.

252
00:28:45,800 --> 00:28:47,200
Let's say we never had this talk.

253
00:28:48,160 --> 00:28:49,400
Look closely.

254
00:28:50,440 --> 00:28:52,720
You'll be set for the rest of your life.

255
00:28:53,400 --> 00:28:56,400
You know I fought alongside him.

256
00:28:56,920 --> 00:28:58,200
Back when I took a bullet,

257
00:28:59,640 --> 00:29:01,760
he carried me
out of the border on his back.

258
00:29:02,360 --> 00:29:05,080
And what if today he's the one
carrying you to your grave?

259
00:29:11,160 --> 00:29:12,200
The word "friendship"

260
00:29:13,800 --> 00:29:16,040
won't feed your kids.

261
00:29:17,400 --> 00:29:18,560
You know what happens

262
00:29:19,800 --> 00:29:21,880
when people are dirt poor?

263
00:29:23,240 --> 00:29:25,200
They don't have an ounce of dignity left.

264
00:29:26,640 --> 00:29:28,760
All they'll ask you

265
00:29:29,400 --> 00:29:31,240
is if your family has enough to eat.

266
00:29:35,240 --> 00:29:38,000
If you don't do it, someone else will.

267
00:29:39,240 --> 00:29:40,240
Right?

268
00:29:50,360 --> 00:29:53,760
METHEE: TWO MESSAGES

269
00:29:59,920 --> 00:30:01,360
<i>I found some intel</i>

270
00:30:02,040 --> 00:30:04,480
<i>on who’s backing Seehan.</i>

271
00:30:24,880 --> 00:30:27,800
If you were coming,
you should have informed me in advance.

272
00:30:28,400 --> 00:30:32,240
I was planning to take you all out
for dinner in Hong Kong.

273
00:30:40,880 --> 00:30:43,520
No need. We're already here.

274
00:30:46,440 --> 00:30:48,280
Bring out the food.

275
00:30:49,240 --> 00:30:52,480
We didn't come here to eat.
We came to talk.

276
00:30:54,920 --> 00:30:56,400
Let's get straight to the point.

277
00:30:58,080 --> 00:31:01,760
With Tongyang dead,
the investigation is targeting you.

278
00:31:01,840 --> 00:31:05,360
I tried my best to find evidence

279
00:31:05,440 --> 00:31:07,560
to clear your name, but it's tough,

280
00:31:07,640 --> 00:31:10,840
because Tongyang's main rival

281
00:31:10,920 --> 00:31:12,320
was you.

282
00:31:13,960 --> 00:31:15,440
Whoever you hired for the hit,

283
00:31:16,520 --> 00:31:18,360
you should have consulted me first.

284
00:31:18,440 --> 00:31:20,200
Well…

285
00:31:21,120 --> 00:31:24,280
I figured Gun has been out
of the force for a long time, sir.

286
00:31:24,920 --> 00:31:28,520
Whatever he does
shouldn't bring trouble to you.

287
00:31:28,600 --> 00:31:31,320
But you can't just do whatever you want.

288
00:31:33,760 --> 00:31:35,040
Killing someone these days

289
00:31:35,120 --> 00:31:37,560
isn't as easy as it used to be.

290
00:31:38,680 --> 00:31:40,360
Even if he left official service,

291
00:31:41,200 --> 00:31:43,240
his old department is still responsible.

292
00:31:43,880 --> 00:31:46,480
And the Military Committee
is currently looking into it.

293
00:31:47,280 --> 00:31:48,800
My department

294
00:31:49,720 --> 00:31:51,320
might get its budget slashed,

295
00:31:52,040 --> 00:31:53,080
or worse,

296
00:31:54,000 --> 00:31:55,760
I might be removed from my post.

297
00:31:55,840 --> 00:31:59,080
Do you realize
you're putting everyone in jeopardy?

298
00:32:01,080 --> 00:32:04,880
I assure you,
I won't cause trouble for any of you.

299
00:32:06,680 --> 00:32:08,080
But you messed up this time.

300
00:32:08,760 --> 00:32:11,960
And now it's getting out of hand.

301
00:32:13,800 --> 00:32:15,040
All of us

302
00:32:16,000 --> 00:32:18,160
will have to use
much more leverage than before.

303
00:32:35,640 --> 00:32:36,640
I sincerely apologize.

304
00:32:39,080 --> 00:32:40,280
I'm deeply sorry.

305
00:32:41,760 --> 00:32:43,480
I'm truly sorry, sir.

306
00:32:53,560 --> 00:32:54,480
Well.

307
00:32:55,400 --> 00:32:56,720
In that case, we'll talk later.

308
00:32:58,600 --> 00:33:01,640
Thank you so much
for taking the time to come.

309
00:33:01,720 --> 00:33:04,440
I'll say goodbye to you here.

310
00:33:04,520 --> 00:33:05,640
Alright.

311
00:33:22,240 --> 00:33:23,800
Street beggars

312
00:33:24,920 --> 00:33:27,280
have more dignity than those scumbags.

313
00:33:46,160 --> 00:33:48,600
<i>They collect their cut</i>
<i>at the end of every month.</i>

314
00:33:49,720 --> 00:33:51,520
<i>I'll investigate</i>
<i>and send you the location.</i>

315
00:34:19,679 --> 00:34:21,840
<i>This place doesn't have parking out front.</i>

316
00:34:22,880 --> 00:34:25,480
<i>He'll have to get out</i>
<i>at the front and walk inside.</i>

317
00:34:25,560 --> 00:34:26,880
<i>Your chance will come</i>

318
00:34:27,840 --> 00:34:29,159
<i>just as he goes inside.</i>

319
00:35:02,800 --> 00:35:04,480
Proceed with the plan, Boss.

320
00:35:06,680 --> 00:35:09,160
Then get your black suits ready
for Gun's funeral.

321
00:35:10,400 --> 00:35:11,880
<i>I love working with professionals.</i>

322
00:35:15,400 --> 00:35:17,520
The world has changed, Boss.

323
00:35:19,920 --> 00:35:21,360
A man has to know how to adapt.

324
00:35:21,880 --> 00:35:24,280
<i>Once it's done,</i>
<i>send me a photo of his body.</i>

325
00:35:24,840 --> 00:35:27,280
<i>I'll save it as my phone wallpaper.</i>

326
00:36:03,960 --> 00:36:05,960
You're still slower than me, Gun.

327
00:36:31,760 --> 00:36:33,320
So it was you who shot me.

328
00:36:41,960 --> 00:36:43,480
You really are tough to kill.

329
00:36:44,200 --> 00:36:45,760
Got any good amulets on you?

330
00:36:46,440 --> 00:36:47,760
Share some with me.

331
00:36:49,000 --> 00:36:50,040
You missed

332
00:36:51,360 --> 00:36:54,560
because of the booze.
Your old habits never change.

333
00:37:02,000 --> 00:37:04,680
You know my family is struggling.
I need money.

334
00:37:06,040 --> 00:37:07,480
My kid needs to eat.

335
00:37:07,560 --> 00:37:09,240
So you chose to betray me

336
00:37:10,320 --> 00:37:12,680
by taking a contract to kill
the guy who saved your life.

337
00:37:12,760 --> 00:37:16,240
I made that choice so my family could
survive, but I didn't want to kill you.

338
00:37:17,160 --> 00:37:19,240
Because you saved my life
back at the border.

339
00:37:19,880 --> 00:37:22,080
So I intentionally missed your head today.

340
00:37:22,880 --> 00:37:24,120
Listen to me, buddy.

341
00:37:24,200 --> 00:37:26,680
Seehan wants you to work with him.

342
00:37:27,320 --> 00:37:29,560
You and me together,

343
00:37:29,640 --> 00:37:31,640
and we'll be set for life.

344
00:37:33,600 --> 00:37:35,040
<i>Better than working for scumbags</i>

345
00:37:37,000 --> 00:37:38,440
<i>who do nothing but feed off us</i>

346
00:37:39,760 --> 00:37:41,560
<i>and use us as tools</i>

347
00:37:41,640 --> 00:37:43,280
<i>to line their pockets.</i>

348
00:37:44,280 --> 00:37:46,240
<i>Seehan's a piece of work,</i>

349
00:37:46,320 --> 00:37:47,960
<i>but at least he shares.</i>

350
00:37:48,760 --> 00:37:51,160
-Come. Cheers.
-Cheers.

351
00:37:52,480 --> 00:37:53,320
To our prosperity.

352
00:37:56,120 --> 00:37:57,040
I know

353
00:37:58,000 --> 00:38:00,400
you left the force
because you hated the corrupt system.

354
00:38:01,040 --> 00:38:03,040
Why don't you use them to your advantage?

355
00:38:04,720 --> 00:38:06,880
You want me to serve a scammer boss

356
00:38:06,960 --> 00:38:09,160
who steals money and ruins lives?

357
00:38:09,240 --> 00:38:11,040
Even if Seehan doesn't do it,

358
00:38:11,120 --> 00:38:13,480
someone else will anyway.

359
00:38:14,640 --> 00:38:17,360
Gun, since you can't stop them,

360
00:38:17,440 --> 00:38:19,680
why not use them to your advantage?

361
00:38:21,040 --> 00:38:22,400
But he killed my grandma.

362
00:38:27,000 --> 00:38:29,760
I'm sorry about your grandma.

363
00:38:30,640 --> 00:38:34,200
But nothing can bring back the dead.

364
00:38:37,400 --> 00:38:39,040
How can you fight them alone?

365
00:38:40,280 --> 00:38:41,400
Trust me, buddy.

366
00:38:43,320 --> 00:38:46,360
You and I should team up.

367
00:38:49,680 --> 00:38:50,720
Do you know

368
00:38:51,680 --> 00:38:53,080
what's scarier than money?

369
00:38:55,400 --> 00:38:57,960
It's people who think
this bullshit is normal.

370
00:38:59,320 --> 00:39:01,880
No wonder this world
never gets any better.

371
00:39:03,240 --> 00:39:04,760
Because people who think like you

372
00:39:05,880 --> 00:39:07,360
are worse than a plague.

373
00:39:39,480 --> 00:39:41,240
I think Gun must have had help.

374
00:39:42,080 --> 00:39:44,200
<i>He wouldn't have survived</i>
<i>this long working alone.</i>

375
00:39:48,440 --> 00:39:49,760
Can I trust you?

376
00:39:51,960 --> 00:39:52,960
Answer me.

377
00:39:54,760 --> 00:39:56,360
We've located Gun, sir.

378
00:39:56,440 --> 00:40:00,080
Paisan, use the law to crush him.

379
00:40:00,160 --> 00:40:02,360
Help. Help!

380
00:40:03,280 --> 00:40:04,280
Shoot to kill.

381
00:40:11,920 --> 00:40:13,520
Set. Set.

382
00:40:24,240 --> 00:40:25,600
Good, good. Okay.

383
00:40:29,960 --> 00:40:32,680
-Speed.
-Scene nine, take two.

384
00:40:32,760 --> 00:40:34,160
And…

385
00:40:36,280 --> 00:40:39,680
-Set.
-Low shot. And… Action!

386
00:40:54,160 --> 00:40:55,440
Cut!

387
00:40:57,080 --> 00:40:58,360
‎It came off.

388
00:41:38,640 --> 00:41:40,680
Subtitle translation by: Anan Pratchayakul
